  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Production higher-weight Hecke matrices now return owned generated FmpqMatrix resources. The typed traversal performs each exact contribution through one generic declared FLINT add-scaled-entry operation, removing uniform limb capacities, retries, packed result export, and host rational reconstruction. Native and same-source dynamic results are differential against the legacy FLINT oracle across level 11 T_101 and signed level-1000 weight-4/6 cases. The complete public typed route measures 2.64 ms versus 1.85 ms for the oracle on the 16-vCPU AMD EPYC host, with only 640 KiB peak-RSS growth across the timed batch and sanitizer-backed resource lifecycle coverage.",
    "risks": [
      "The modular slice required a generic shared FFI primitive, so the current lane checker cannot express the authorized cross-lane claims in one coherent task even though architecture checks pass.",
      "The declaration is marked wasm-compatible, but this lane did not rebuild the browser FLINT artifact."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Review and integrate the combined modular-forms and shared-FFI slice; split by lane during merge only if repository policy requires it.",
      "Use the generic scaled-entry primitive for other exact typed traversals that accumulate into FLINT-owned rational matrices."
    ]
  }
